## Transformations & Actions

### DataFrame Transformations

**DataFrame-Specific Transformations:**

```python
# withColumn: Add/modify column
df = df.withColumn("yearly_bonus", col("salary") * 0.1)

# withColumnRenamed: Rename column
df = df.withColumnRenamed("salary", "annual_salary")

# drop: Remove column
df = df.drop("bonus")

# dropDuplicates: Remove duplicates
df_unique = df.dropDuplicates()
df_unique = df.dropDuplicates(["name"])  # Based on specific columns

# fillna: Fill NULL values
df = df.fillna(0)
df = df.fillna({"salary": 50000, "age": 30})

# cast: Change data type
df = df.withColumn("age", col("age").cast(IntegerType()))

# collect_list: Aggregate into list
from pyspark.sql.functions import collect_list, collect_set
df.groupBy("department").agg(collect_list("name")).show()
df.groupBy("department").agg(collect_set("name")).show()  # Unique
```

**Join Operations:**
```python
df1 = spark.createDataFrame([("John", 1), ("Jane", 2)], ["name", "emp_id"])
df2 = spark.createDataFrame([(1, "Sales"), (2, "IT")], ["emp_id", "dept"])

# Inner join (default)
result = df1.join(df2, on="emp_id")

# Left outer join
result = df1.join(df2, on="emp_id", how="left")

# Right outer join
result = df1.join(df2, on="emp_id", how="right")

# Full outer join
result = df1.join(df2, on="emp_id", how="full")

# Cross join (Cartesian product)
result = df1.crossJoin(df2)
```

**Set Operations:**
```python
df1 = spark.createDataFrame([("John",), ("Jane",)], ["name"])
df2 = spark.createDataFrame([("Jane",), ("Bob",)], ["name"])

# Union
result = df1.union(df2)
# Result: John, Jane, Jane, Bob

# Union all (explicit)
result = df1.unionByName(df2)

# Intersect
result = df1.intersect(df2)
# Result: Jane

# Except (difference)
result = df1.except(df2)
# Result: John
```

### DataFrame Actions

```python
# collect: Return to driver
data = df.collect()

# show: Display
df.show(20, truncate=False)

# count: Count rows
row_count = df.count()

# first: First row
first_row = df.first()

# take: First n rows
first_five = df.take(5)

# write: Save to storage
df.write.mode("overwrite").csv("path/to/output")
df.write.mode("append").parquet("path/to/output")
df.write.saveAsTable("my_table")

# explain: Show execution plan
df.explain(extended=True)

# toPandas: Convert to pandas DataFrame
pandas_df = df.toPandas()

# rdd: Convert back to RDD
rdd = df.rdd
```

