## Data Sources & I/O

### Reading Data

```python
# CSV
df = spark.read \
    .option("header", "true") \
    .option("inferSchema", "true") \
    .option("sep", ",") \
    .csv("path/to/file.csv")

# JSON
df = spark.read \
    .option("multiLine", "true") \
    .json("path/to/file.json")

# Parquet (Columnar format - recommended)
df = spark.read.parquet("path/to/file.parquet")

# ORC
df = spark.read.orc("path/to/file.orc")

# Text
df = spark.read.text("path/to/file.txt")

# Binary
df = spark.read.format("binaryFile").load("path/to/binary")

# Avro
df = spark.read.format("avro").load("path/to/file.avro")

# Delta (Lakehouse format)
df = spark.read.format("delta").load("path/to/delta")
```

### Writing Data

```python
# Write modes
# overwrite: Replace entire file
# append: Add to existing file
# ignore: Skip if exists
# error: Throw error if exists

# CSV
df.write.mode("overwrite") \
    .option("header", "true") \
    .option("sep", ",") \
    .csv("path/to/output.csv")

# Parquet
df.write.mode("overwrite").parquet("path/to/output.parquet")

# JSON
df.write.mode("overwrite").json("path/to/output.json")

# ORC
df.write.mode("overwrite").orc("path/to/output.orc")

# Delta
df.write.mode("overwrite").format("delta").save("path/to/delta")

# Partitioned write
df.write.partitionBy("year", "month") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .parquet("path/to/output")

# Bucketed write
df.write.bucketBy(10, "id") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .parquet("path/to/output")
```

### Working with Different Formats

**Parquet (Best for analytics):**
```python
# Advantages: Columnar format, compression, schema preservation
df.write.parquet("hdfs://path/to/data.parquet")

# Reading specific columns (pushdown)
df = spark.read.parquet("hdfs://path/to/data.parquet")
df.select("name", "age").show()  # Only reads these columns
```

**Delta Lake (ACID transactions):**
```python
# Write
df.write.format("delta").mode("overwrite").save("path/to/delta")

# Read
df = spark.read.format("delta").load("path/to/delta")

# Update
spark.sql("""
    UPDATE delta.`path/to/delta`
    SET salary = salary * 1.1
    WHERE age > 30
""")

# Delete
spark.sql("""
    DELETE FROM delta.`path/to/delta`
    WHERE status = 'INACTIVE'
""")

# Time travel
df = spark.read.format("delta").option("versionAsOf", 1).load("path/to/delta")
```

